WEBVTT

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:11.740
Right!

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.260
Sorry I kept you waiting!

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.510
It's just you here, Natsuki?

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.100
Where's everyone else?

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.690
Um, Karin is...

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.060
I-It's due today?!

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.690
She went to turn in a handout
that she had forgotten was due.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.530
I see.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.320
So what about the other two?

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:19.070
We don't want anything to happen to you.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.660
I'll escort you to the faculty room.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.950
They were worried about her, so they tagged along.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.790
They coddle her too much.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:29.080
Well, until they get back, why don't
we play Word Chain or something?

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.380
Playing Word Chain because we're bored almost
seems too tame, compared to your usual ideas.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.510
I thought you'd say that!

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.460
Huh?

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.340
But what we're about to play is
no ordinary game of Word Chain!

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.720
We'll be using these Taboo Cards!

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.310
Taboo Cards?!

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.230
Taboo Card Rules!

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.900
Before the game starts, each player
writes a word of their choice on a card,

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.690
then lays it facedown.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.360
This word is considered taboo
throughout the game and,

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.030
like a word ending with "n," it ends the game.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.820
I get it.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:05.660
You have to avoid using the word
on your opponent's Taboo Card,

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.830
while also luring the opponent into
saying the word on your own card.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.420
And one more thing...

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.000
All games need some kind of risk and return.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.550
If you win, Natsuki,
I'll give you something good.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.090
Something good?

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.590
F-Fine.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.850
Then, if I lose...

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.220
Of course, if you lose...

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.520
you have to eat spaghetti through your nose!

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.980
Her tastes in game penalties are so old-fashioned!

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.570
This Taboo Card holds the key to my victory.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.990
But what word should I write?

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.410
I guess I should just pick one that
I wouldn't accidentally say myself...

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.880
Okay, are you all ready?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.550
Once you've written down your
word, you can't change it.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.340
It may even be possible

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.680
that the game is already
decided the moment we both

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.140
choose our taboo words.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.510
We won't know who wins until we play.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.520
It's still Word Chain, after all.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.730
We're both playing by the same terms.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.730
Let's go over the rules!

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.650
The basic rules are the same
as standard Word Chain.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.360
If you use a word ending in "n," you lose!

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.370
If you use the words written
on either Taboo Card, you lose!

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.120
The time limit is one minute per turn.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.500
If you exceed that, you lose!

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.250
Taboo Card, set!

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.370
Word Chain, in!

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.580
I'll go first,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:38.750
Wha—

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.260
Y-You took the first turn by force!

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.720
Don't be so naïve, Natsuki!

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.880
The game's already begun!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.260
It's my turn!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:47.510
Risuzaru<i> (squirrel monkey)</i>!

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.350
A Lead-off Switchup!

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:54.890
As the saying goes: "Shiritori starts with 'pa.'"

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:58.480
Shiritori <i>(Word Chain),</i>  ringo <i>(apple), </i>gorira <i>(gorilla),</i>

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.820
and rappa (trumpet)<i> is the standard
opening pattern for a Word Chain.</i>

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.030
To actively make a change to that pattern...

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.360
is called a "Pattern Switchup."

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:12.620
One plan of attack is to lead off
with a word other than "apple."

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.830
This is known as a "Lead-off Switchup."

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.790
The goal is to confuse any opponent
prepared to respond with "gorilla,"

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.300
upsetting their rhythm early on.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.460
Of course.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.720
We're playing with Taboo Card rules.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.760
If I had predicted that she'd
lead off with the usual pattern

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.430
and selected "apple" as my taboo word,

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.100
that would've ended the game right then and there.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.730
Hence the Lead-off Switchup!

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.650
R-Ruretto<i> (roulette)</i>.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:39.610
Tonneru<i> (tunnel)</i>.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.190
Sakura responds in a flash!

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:44.940
Ruuzu sokkusu <i>(loose socks)</i>.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:45.820
Sutooru <i>(stole)</i>.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.700
Here, Natsuki begins to suspect something's up...

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.240
Sutooru<i> (stole)</i>.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.120
Now, her suspicion turns to certainty.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.700
This is...

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.500
a "Ru" Offensive!

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.290
The "Ru" Offensive: a strategy that takes advantage

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.920
of the fact that there are far fewer words
beginning with "ru" than ending with "ru,"

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.260
and thus using only words ending in "ru."

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:10.510
There are other, similar strategies,
such as the "Ri" Offensive.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:16.270
That means Sakura's taboo
word probably starts with "ru."

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:19.310
I blurted out "roulette" earlier
without thinking about it,

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:22.480
but maybe I should stick with more
obscure words when possible.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:06:59.810
I'm running out of words!

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.810
The time limit of one minute per turn

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.070
clearly has Natsuki on the ropes.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:09.700
Pressure can have a strikingly negative
effect on a person's judgment.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.450
Words that she should know fail to come to her!

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:18.540
At this rate, whether she says Sakura's
taboo word or breaks the time limit...

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.080
it's only a matter of time.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.580
I guess it's time...

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.790
But Natsuki had a plan!

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:26.750
Counter

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.260
It was a "Counter"!

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:28.630
Counter

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.590
The "Ru" Offensive,

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.930
which attacks with a specific syllable,
has one fatal weakness.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.680
This is called the Counter.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.770
After exhausting the vocabulary of words that begin with "ru,"

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.140
returning with a word that both starts and ends with "ru"

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:44.900
turns your opponent's offensive back on them!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.530
The word that Natsuki has kept up her sleeve!

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:51.860
That word is:

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:53.410
Ruuru (rule)<i>!</i>

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:54.110
Ru—

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.450
But the moment she opened her mouth,

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.450
a jolt of electricity hit Natsuki!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.160
Call it intuition or instinct!

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:06.210
Halted by that momentary chill,
Natsuki swallowed the word!

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:09.590
I get it.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.930
The word that Sakura
wrote on her Taboo Card was...

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:13.970
Rule!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.010
She wasn't using her Taboo
Card to defeat me directly.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.470
She did it stop me from countering her "Ru" Offensive!

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.600
Her guess was correct.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.480
So you've caught on?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.650
But it's too late, Natsuki.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.480
The moment you accepted this game, you'd already...

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.190
fallen into my trap!

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:38.870
Isn't that a relief?

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.080
You got your handout turned in.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:41.870
Yes!

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.750
Do you think Sakura has turned up yet?

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.630
I'm sure she's there by now.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:50.340
So Natsuki and Sakura are in there by themselves?

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:54.760
By themselves?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.260
Why don't we go grab some tea before we head back?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.430
Why do you want to give them more time alone?

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:09.820
The reason most Word Chain games take place

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.240
is to kill time.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:18.660
In most cases, Word Chain is not played competitively.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.240
Rather, the intent is simply to keep
the game going as long as possible.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:27.620
I bet you've only ever played that dull
form of Word Chain, right, Natsuki?

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.460
Let me teach you...

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.880
the Word Chain where you crush your opponent!

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.800
How...

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:42.180
How could this turn into such a war of attrition?

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:45.930
My Counter Word against
Sakura's "Ru" Offensive,

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.150
"Rule," has been taken from me.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.860
I'm definitely going to lose now...

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.150
Runesansu <i>(Renaissance)</i>.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:52.860
Sumairu <i>(smile)</i>.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:54.990
Ru...

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.700
Think! Isn't there anything?!

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.990
Any word that can break this deadlock?!

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.450
Rua, rui, ruu, rue...

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.000
Leaf through the dictionary of my mind!

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.580
Well, think long and hard.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:12.000
As long as I respond instantly
to anything you throw at me,

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.590
you only get sixty seconds to think.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.340
You have to stay calm, at the very least.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:24.470
The more pressured you feel when backed
into a corner, the faster time seems to pass.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:36.280
Ru... Ruuputai <i>(bolo tie)</i>.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.360
Inisharu <i>(initial)</i>.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.530
The time limit approaches!

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.160
The penalty hangs over her head!

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:46.540
Olive Oil... Nose-paghetti...
Peperoncino... Carbonara... Al Dente...

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:51.540
But the severity of the situation,
contrary to Sakura's expectations...

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.840
has given Natsuki a flash of insight!

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:56.960
That's it!

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:00.760
I've got a word that begins and
ends with "ru," other than "rule"!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.760
To break out of the "Ru" Offensive...

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:05.140
A Counter Word!

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:07.850
Now it's my turn!

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.430
Ruuburu <i>(ruble)</i>!

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:20.070
Ruble?!

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:23.160
I've won.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.120
Just kidding!

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:27.990
Runowaaru <i>(Renoir)</i>.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:48.270
Natsuki. You fought hard.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:53.310
I never expected you to find a Counter Word
other than "rule" in a situation like that.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.650
You're everything I'd expect of a junior in my club.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:12:01.400
But I'd already prepared several
countermeasures to the counter.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.450
That should crush Natsuki's spirit.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.030
I've won!

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.460
Wha—

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.040
Now it's my turn!

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:16.130
Why?!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.540
How can you still stand?!

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.550
Why won't you just admit defeat?!

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.130
Because I am...

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.930
I am a Word Chainist!

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.340
What's that?! I've never heard that title before!

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:27.300
What do I do?

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:30.390
I didn't crush her spirit enough, and it
seems to have revved her up even more!

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.810
Ruijiana-shuu <i>(Louisiana State)</i>!

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.350
"U"? "U," huh?

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:37.690
"U"?

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:38.980
What?

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:42.440
I've already used "wool" and
"wedding bell" and "sea-firefly"...

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:46.070
"U..." Strange, I can't think of anything.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.120
Well, as you wish.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.120
I'll play it safe.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.830
After all, even if Natsuki
comes at me with "ru,"

00:12:56.830 --> 00:13:00.880
I still have a full stock of Counter Words.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:02.710
Umigame <i>(sea turtle)</i>.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:06.590
There! Now, come at me with meeru (mail)<i></i>

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.090
Meifurawaagou <i>(The Mayflower)</i>.

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.140
Another "u"?

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:13.180
Kyouryuu <i>(dinosaur)</i>.

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:13.930
Usagi <i>(rabbit)</i>.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.440
Gyuunyuu <i>(milk)</i>.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:17.940
I get it.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:22.900
I've exhausted all the words that
start with "u" and end with "ru."

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:23.860
In other words,

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.900
as long as she keeps responding with "u,"

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.370
I can't relaunch my "Ru" Offensive.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:32.490
But there are still tons of
words that start with "u."

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:36.410
In this situation, Natsuki needs
to keep responding with "u" endings,

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:37.960
which means she's the one at a disadvantage.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.500
Uruudoshi <i>(leap year)</i>.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.460
Shodou <i>(calligraphy)</i>.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:42.630
Wait a minute!

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.170
Come to think of it,

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:48.800
Natsuki added "daitouryou" (president)<i>
when just "Roosevelt" would have done,</i>

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.760
and added "shuu" (state) <i>when just
"Louisiana" would have sufficed...</i>

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.810
Was she... trying to make me say words starting with "u"?!

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.440
Is it possible...

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.480
that Natsuki's taboo word
is a word that starts with a "u"?!

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.490
When I consider that possibility,

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:09.990
maybe I should focus on more
obscure words when possible...

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.740
Umibouzu<i> (sea monster)</i>.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.000
Sakura.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.250
You just said "umibouzu," didn't you?

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:19.040
Huh?

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:20.790
Wha—

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.170
Taboo Card, open!

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:24.670
What?!

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:27.550
The taboo word I chose was:

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:29.800
"Umibouzu"!

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:34.350
Wh-Why'd you choose a word like that?!

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.430
It was a coincidence, actually.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:41.190
I guess I should just pick one that
I wouldn't accidentally say myself...

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.360
Th-That's the only reason?!

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.820
No doubt about it, it was sheer coincidence.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:50.200
Born from the short yet rich time they've spent together,

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.330
an unconscious synchronization of
their thought patterns took place!

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.580
It was almost an inevitability!

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:01.460
The two of them, both drawn to a single word!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:02.460
Oh, no!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:06.090
Are you saying that Natsuki's
thoughts and mine have fused?!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:10.050
I execute a direct attack on
my opponent with "umibouzu"!

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:16.720
Poseidon Hammer!

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.560
Well, Sakura...

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:26.190
Hand over what you promised me.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:28.490
Your "something good."

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:35.490
We're back!

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.210
Natsuki, where'd that come from?

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.210
I love it!

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:44.330
It's so cute!

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:46.130
This is Sakura's, right?

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:48.460
Did she give it to you? Did she, huh?

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.470
Well? What happened?

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:51.720
Nothing happened.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:54.640
For the first time in her life,

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.810
Natsuki has tasted the humiliation of victory.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.270
Seal Summoning!

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:11.950
Now then!

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.780
We're all here, right?

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:14.740
Okay!

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:17.200
Who knows what tomorrow is?

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:17.910
I do!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.580
It's Natsuki's birthday!

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:20.700
Excellent!

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.710
In view of that, today...

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:27.880
we're going to have a meeting to plan
Natsuki's surprise birthday party!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.050
Wait! I'm sitting right here!

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.970
Okay, everyone!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:43.890
Throw out lots of great ideas for things
that'll surprise and delight Natsuki!

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:47.310
She's just going on with this! What am I supposed to do?

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.230
That's difficult.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:56.280
Natsuki probably already expects
that we'll all want to celebrate with her.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.450
That's because the secret's already out.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:03.200
Even if she acts calm, her thing will be wagging back and forth!

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:05.080
I hear you, I hear you!

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.080
So cute!

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.500
No, no, it does not<i> wag!</i>

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:10.340
Why are you treating it like a dog's tail?!

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:13.840
A silly little surprise party won't really surprise her.

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:17.340
Actually, it won't surprise me
because I already know about it.

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.340
Well?

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:20.100
Does anyone have any good ideas?

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.010
I do!

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:24.100
I think we should make some handicrafts.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:24.980
Handicrafts?

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.600
You know...

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.650
We could cut strips of colored paper,

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.980
make chains out of them, and make flowers.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:35.990
They've changed the point of the meeting...

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.240
Why don't we pop some crackers?

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.200
Yeah! They're good for parties!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.950
But if we're throwing a party,

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.250
I think something more extravagant
would surprise her more.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:46.960
That's true.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.710
Something more extravagant...

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:52.710
I know! Let's set off fireworks!

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.510
That's going way over the top!

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:55.920
I like it!

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:57.180
Let's go extravagant!

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:58.760
No, no, no, no...

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:02.390
For food, we can order room
service from my family's hotel!

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:03.100
Huh?!

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.930
They'll even deliver to the club room?!

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.270
A feast simply <i>has</i> to have
beefsteak, don't you think?

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.520
Beefsteak?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.060
Oh, do they have dessert, too?

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.980
I love desserts with kiwi in them!

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:14.530
They're all just listing things they like...

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:15.690
I know!

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.780
You can't forget the cake, either!

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.620
Right, that's fundamental!

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:22.530
Natsuki does love sweet things.

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:25.580
Let's get a strawberry cake! A big one!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:27.960
Sounds good.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.960
The cake and the staging will get her excited...

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:33.800
Then, we'll all cry out "happy birthday!"

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:35.050
Okay, okay!

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:37.260
This'll be the perfect surprise party!

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:40.300
Yes, I think that'll do it.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:44.350
By the way, Natsuki, do you think
you'd be surprised by all of this?

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.310
Of course not!

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.850
If you give away the whole thing,
there's nothing left to surprise me!

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.190
And then, the next day...

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:54.270
I'm so excited for your surprise party, Natsuki.

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:55.940
Y-Yeah...

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:59.820
Karin. You know what the word
"surprise" means, don't you?

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:01.700
I can't wait!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.340
It's huge!

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.420
What's with the colossal scale?!

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:20.260
It's bigger than the door!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.930
H-How did you get it in here?

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:25.930
We brought the ingredients inside
and made it in the room!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:27.520
Is it a ship in a bottle?!

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:30.940
What? What's that sound?

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:33.860
Fireworks!

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.770
You really set off fireworks?!

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:38.570
But you went to all that trouble,

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.530
and we can't even see them in here...

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:42.910
Well, when you launch fireworks in the daytime,

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.820
all you can see is smoke anyway, so it's no big deal.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:46.780
Then, why did you set them off during the day?!

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.710
Did you make these, Karin?

00:19:56.710 --> 00:20:00.170
After the meeting yesterday,
we all hung them up together.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.380
Also, take a look outside!

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:05.430
This last surprise is amazing, so let your hopes soar!

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:06.760
Yeah.

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:10.390
Getting someone's hopes up is part
of the ABCs of a surprise party.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:15.100
Hopes... ABCs?

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:19.230
This is...

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.260
What's that?

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.510
Who's Natsuki?

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.010
Incredible!

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:32.200
Kitsune<i> (fox)</i>!

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:32.990
Neko <i>(cat)</i>!

00:22:32.990 --> 00:22:33.990
Koori <i>(ice)</i>!

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:36.500
"Ri?!" "Ri," "ri..."

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:39.170
Karin, try this.

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:41.290
Ah! Ribon <i>(ribbon)</i>!

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:47.220
Hey, guys, did you know?

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:51.300
The mating process of the great
gray slug is a grappling match!

00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:54.430
Sounds hot and steamy, doesn't it?!

00:22:57.350 --> 00:22:58.810
And three others!
